(4469147, 643137, 29011, '<td valign="top">This is great. So refreshing and fun. Seeing how the bottle is empty at the bottom part, going all the way out to the model''s face is just excellent. The only nitpick is the little bit of red peaking out from the model''s clothing, and the clothing rippling on the torso. Still, a super shot.</td>', 'This is great. So refreshing and fun. Seeing how the bottle is empty at the bottom part, going all the way out to the model''s face is just excellent. The only nitpick is the little bit of red peaking out from the model''s clothing, and the clothing rippling on the torso. Still, a super shot.', '2008-02-07 19:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(4469152, 641881, 77196, '<td valign="top">Next time, try opening the bottom of the box, leaving the top pristine, rather than with the ears sticking up on either side. For me, a bit more scotch in the glass would have been better. Some people sure have to go a long way to find something to criticize!</td>', 'Next time, try opening the bottom of the box, leaving the top pristine, rather than with the ears sticking up on either side. For me, a bit more scotch in the glass would have been better. Some people sure have to go a long way to find something to criticize!', '2008-02-07 19:10:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4469153, 642278, 29011, '<td valign="top">Flawless really. If it where advanced I''d be tempted to clone out the line in the floor but this is wonderful for basic. Very pro looking. Love the lighting, composition, pose. Looks a lot like Idnic''s portrait work. The use of the corner is way excellent. Something I want to try in portrait photography after reading more about it in a recent issue of the Rangefinder mag, or was it After Capture. Don''t remember exactly, but it was from either.</td>', 'Flawless really. If it where advanced I''d be tempted to clone out the line in the floor but this is wonderful for basic. Very pro looking. Love the lighting, composition, pose. Looks a lot like Idnic''s portrait work. The use of the corner is way excellent. Something I want to try in portrait photography after reading more about it in a recent issue of the Rangefinder mag, or was it After Capture. Don''t remember exactly, but it was from either.', '2008-02-07 19:10:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(4469159, 643188, 77196, '<td valign="top">The OOF cap drops this from a spectacular shot to a no show for me. The pink background (nice and even) gives it the essence, and the blurred cap just stands out in stark contrast to the rest of the image''s feel. 6</td>', 'The OOF cap drops this from a spectacular shot to a no show for me. The pink background (nice and even) gives it the essence, and the blurred cap just stands out in stark contrast to the rest of the image''s feel. 6', '2008-02-07 19:13:16.000000', NULL, 1),
