(4482711, 641180, 29513, '<td valign="top">First, thanks, everyone, for taking the time and trouble to vote and comment.<br/> <br/>This is a picture of an art glass sphere about 2 inches in diameter.  It looks like a planet to me and the artist actually calls them planets.  Here is a link to a different crop of the same raw image as I used here:  <a href="//www.pbase.com/outland/image/92397451/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.pbase.com/outland/image/92397451/</a> <br/> <br/>I picked an angle with the spiral feature showing so that it would be obvious that it wasn''t Earth.  In fact, I thought of using "To Slip The Surly Bonds Of &lt;YourPlanes''sNameHere&gt;. . ." as the title.<br/> <br/>Thanks again.</td>', 'First, thanks, everyone, for taking the time and trouble to vote and comment. This is a picture of an art glass sphere about 2 inches in diameter.  It looks like a planet to me and the artist actually calls them planets.  Here is a link to a different crop of the same raw image as I used here:  //www.pbase.com/outland/image/92397451/  I picked an angle with the spiral feature showing so that it would be obvious that it wasn''t Earth.  In fact, I thought of using "To Slip The Surly Bonds Of <YourPlanes''sNameHere>. . ." as the title. Thanks again.', '2008-02-13 08:20:18.000000', NULL, 0),
