(4488115, 642570, 89859, '<td valign="top">I''d like to thank everyone for their comments.  I took this shot at a car show.  Unfortunately, I was unable to get close enough to shoot straight down on the hood.  So, while it might not look like it from the photo, there is a fairly large distance difference between the top of the logo and the bottom.  I didn''t want to use a flash, which would have changed the color.  I couldn''t use a tripod.  So all these things worked to make for a very narrow depth of field.  You can''t tell from this reduced photo, but looking at the original, the specs of dust right above the R in Lambroghini are in sharp focus but the bull is not.  I should have manually focused on a spot between the lettering and the bull and maybe the results would have been more acceptable.  I would have liked to have gotten rid of the reflections, which were from the overhead illumination at the convention center.  But to do that would have required more than basic editing.<br/> <br/>For those who asked for more pictures of this car, here are some:<br/><a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/sss_philly_car_show_2008/2242594091/sizes/o/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lambo pic 1</a> <br/><a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/sss_philly_car_show_2008/2243388596/sizes/o/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lambo pic 2</a> <br/><a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/sss_philly_car_show_2008/2242595225/sizes/o/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lambo pic 3</a> <br/> <br/>And if anyone is interested in seeing a lot of pictures of the Philly car show, they''re here:<br/><a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/sss_philly_car_show_2008/show/with/2243388936/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Philadelphia Auto Show 2008</a> <br/>But please, don''t be too critical.  I was mostly in "snapshot" mode, not creative mode.  There are a some shots I really do like that I think could stand up to a critique.  But most are just eh.<br/> <br/>Thanks again and hopefully I''ll do better next time.</td>', 'I''d like to thank everyone for their comments.  I took this shot at a car show.  Unfortunately, I was unable to get close enough to shoot straight down on the hood.  So, while it might not look like it from the photo, there is a fairly large distance difference between the top of the logo and the bottom.  I didn''t want to use a flash, which would have changed the color.  I couldn''t use a tripod.  So all these things worked to make for a very narrow depth of field.  You can''t tell from this reduced photo, but looking at the original, the specs of dust right above the R in Lambroghini are in sharp focus but the bull is not.  I should have manually focused on a spot between the lettering and the bull and maybe the results would have been more acceptable.  I would have liked to have gotten rid of the reflections, which were from the overhead illumination at the convention center.  But to do that would have required more than basic editing. For those who asked for more pictures of this car, here are some:Lambo pic 1 Lambo pic 2 Lambo pic 3  And if anyone is interested in seeing a lot of pictures of the Philly car show, they''re here:Philadelphia Auto Show 2008 But please, don''t be too critical.  I was mostly in "snapshot" mode, not creative mode.  There are a some shots I really do like that I think could stand up to a critique.  But most are just eh. Thanks again and hopefully I''ll do better next time.', '2008-02-15 04:31:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4488469, 642702, 61961, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> Sorry but half of this shot is Out Of Focus. That means your technicals are bad. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hehe.  Joker.  <br/> <br/>I think what kept me from scoring this higher than I did (which was 8) was the cat''s body language.  On first impression it seemed the cat did not want to be there and was looking at the milk suspiciously. <br/> <br/>PS: <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=640614" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640614.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640614.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640614.jpg"/></a> <br/>Same Siamese? :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Sorry but half of this shot is Out Of Focus. That means your technicals are bad.  Hehe.  Joker.   I think what kept me from scoring this higher than I did (which was 8) was the cat''s body language.  On first impression it seemed the cat did not want to be there and was looking at the milk suspiciously.  PS:  Same Siamese? :-)', '2008-02-15 09:37:49.000000', NULL, 0),
